  <main class="page">
    <header class="portfolio-header">
      <h1>Portfolio</h1>
      <p class="portfolio-intro">A selection of projects from my Software Development coursework and beyond. Each project reflects hands-on learning in systems programming, web development, and databases.</p>
    </header>

    <!-- ===== SDEV 301 PROJECT — microjam ===== -->
    <section class="section project-card" aria-labelledby="proj-301-title">
      <div class="project-meta">
        <h2 id="proj-301-title">microjam – GBA Game in C++</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="project-body">
        <div class="project-info">
          <p class="project-desc">A game built in C++ for the Game Boy Advance (GBA) as part of Green River College's Cohort 23 Microjam. The project targets real GBA hardware and emulators, covering low-level graphics rendering, audio, and game loop logic — all without a traditional operating system or standard library.</p>

          <div class="project-detail-grid">
            <div>
              <h3>Technologies Used</h3>
              <ul>
                <li>C++ (low-level systems programming)</li>
                <li>GBA hardware architecture</li>
                <li>devkitARM / libgba toolchain</li>
                <li>Makefile build system</li>
                <li>Aseprite (pixel art / sprite assets)</li>
                <li>GitHub Actions (CI)</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3>My Role</h3>
              <p>Contributor on a cohort-wide collaborative game jam. Worked on game logic, sprite/graphics assets, and the build pipeline. Practiced low-level memory management and GBA-specific rendering techniques in a constrained hardware environment.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="project-links">
            <a href="https://github.com/kacastillo/microjam" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn-project">
              <svg aria-hidden="true" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="currentColor"><path d="M8 0C3.58 0 0 3.58 0 8c0 3.54 2.29 6.53 5.47 7.59.4.07.55-.17.55-.38 0-.19-.01-.82-.01-1.49-2.01.37-2.53-.49-2.69-.94-.09-.23-.48-.94-.82-1.13-.28-.15-.68-.52-.01-.53.63-.01 1.08.58 1.23.82.72 1.21 1.87.87 2.33.66.07-.52.28-.87.51-1.07-1.78-.2-3.64-.89-3.64-3.95 0-.87.31-1.59.82-2.15-.08-.2-.36-1.02.08-2.12 0 0 .67-.21 2.2.82.64-.18 1.32-.27 2-.27.68 0 1.36.09 2 .27 1.53-1.04 2.2-.82 2.2-.82.44 1.1.16 1.92.08 2.12.51.56.82 1.27.82 2.15 0 3.07-1.87 3.75-3.65 3.95.29.25.54.73.54 1.48 0 1.07-.01 1.93-.01 2.2 0 .21.15.46.55.38A8.013 8.013 0 0016 8c0-4.42-3.58-8-8-8z"/></svg>
              View on GitHub
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ===== SDEV 305 PROJECT ===== -->
    <section class="section project-card" aria-labelledby="proj-305-title">
      <div class="project-meta">
        <h2 id="proj-305-title">Database-Backed Resume App with MySQL</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="project-body">
        <div class="project-info">
          <p class="project-desc">A full-stack personal resume and guestbook web application that persists all contact form submissions to a MySQL database. Features server-side validation, EJS templating with shared partials, a sortable admin dashboard powered by DataTables, and deployment on Digital Ocean.</p>

          <div class="project-detail-grid">
            <div>
              <h3>Technologies Used</h3>
              <ul>
                <li>Node.js &amp; Express.js</li>
                <li>MySQL 8 via <code>mysql2/promise</code></li>
                <li>EJS templating with partials</li>
                <li>DataTables.js (admin view)</li>
                <li>dotenv for environment config</li>
                <li>Server-side &amp; client-side form validation</li>
                <li>Digital Ocean App Platform</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3>My Role</h3>
              <p>Sole developer — designed and built the full stack from scratch, including the resume layout, contact form with dual validation, confirmation page, admin submission viewer, shared navigation partial, and portfolio page. Deployed to Digital Ocean.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="project-links">
            <a href="https://github.com/kacastillo?tab=repositories" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn-project">
              <svg aria-hidden="true" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="currentColor"><path d="M8 0C3.58 0 0 3.58 0 8c0 3.54 2.29 6.53 5.47 7.59.4.07.55-.17.55-.38 0-.19-.01-.82-.01-1.49-2.01.37-2.53-.49-2.69-.94-.09-.23-.48-.94-.82-1.13-.28-.15-.68-.52-.01-.53.63-.01 1.08.58 1.23.82.72 1.21 1.87.87 2.33.66.07-.52.28-.87.51-1.07-1.78-.2-3.64-.89-3.64-3.95 0-.87.31-1.59.82-2.15-.08-.2-.36-1.02.08-2.12 0 0 .67-.21 2.2.82.64-.18 1.32-.27 2-.27.68 0 1.36.09 2 .27 1.53-1.04 2.2-.82 2.2-.82.44 1.1.16 1.92.08 2.12.51.56.82 1.27.82 2.15 0 3.07-1.87 3.75-3.65 3.95.29.25.54.73.54 1.48 0 1.07-.01 1.93-.01 2.2 0 .21.15.46.55.38A8.013 8.013 0 0016 8c0-4.42-3.58-8-8-8z"/></svg>
              View on GitHub
